BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 413.77 Tm (The most repeated failure is the number moving between the seat map and the payment screen. thumbsuprun recalls the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 398.55 Tm (Rolling Stones run: the venue carried a set general admission price, then buyers reaching the payment step saw it jump) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 383.32 Tm ($50, $70, $90, and plenty paid anyway because nobody expects a carted price to change before checkout) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 368.10 Tm ([TpXJCfuFf4o @ 00:09:44]. Scott Cramer shows a friend's Shania Twain order listed at $227 each turning into $291) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 352.87 Tm (apiece on the final screen, a 30% bump on the very last step of the transaction [kFsH01UthzA @ 00:11:23]. Follow) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 337.65 Tm (The Why documents the queue version from the Oasis reunion: fans watched a standing ticket listed around 135) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 322.42 Tm (pounds, queued for hours, and reached the front to find it over 350, same ticket, same day, with backlash loud enough) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 307.20 Tm (that Britain's competition watchdog investigated [cmeE4rZAlVk @ 00:06:11]. Profit Mechanics explains why the trap) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 291.97 Tm (lands on nearly everyone: a $60 headline becomes $90 once service, facility, order processing and email delivery fees) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 276.75 Tm (appear, and by then the buyer has already committed, so walking away feels like losing the night. Across 20,000 seats,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 261.52 Tm (a $30 fee stack becomes $600,000 collected before a single note is played [p8peX6mgbrw @ 00:03:24]. Every one of) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 246.30 Tm (these is a cost-basis error waiting to happen if the cart price gets logged as the buy price.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 231.07 Tm (The second trap is assuming resale margin survives the fee cascade. Scott Cramer walks it through: a $50 listed ticket) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 215.85 Tm (checks out at $75, so a holder who resells must ask $75 just to break even, the next buyer pays at least another $25 in) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 200.62 Tm (fees, and the platform has now pulled an extra $50 out of one $50 seat, repeating on every transfer after that) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 185.40 Tm ([kFsH01UthzA @ 00:07:45]. Business Made Simple puts both sides on one receipt: list an $80 ticket at $150 and the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 170.17 Tm (buyer sees $187.50 after a 25% buyer fee, while the site often takes a cut from the seller as well [VBp4zpS7F3o @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 154.95 Tm (00:08:42]. Why It Costs flags the floor that gets ignored: a GAO sample averaged secondary fees at 31% of listed price) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 139.72 Tm (before fees, and CRS says weak demand can leave resellers with outright losses, so an expensive listing guarantees) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 124.50 Tm (nothing [tH7bLaJI6ZE @ 00:08:16]. Firstpost shows the downside live on Cowboy Carter: resale collapsing to a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 109.27 Tm (reported $35, more than 3,200 unsold seats on the Los Angeles opening night, over 5,500 still sitting for the New) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 94.05 Tm (Jersey date added for high demand, and nearly half the Atlanta floor open while the platform claimed 94% sold) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 78.82 Tm ([nAgJ_xD_wuE @ 00:02:54]. A superstar name is not the same thing as superstar resale demand.) Tj ET
